{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use","id":1415198,"title":"How often you use...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-23T09:30:23-07:00","id":1415198,"title":"How often you use...","content":"In a game you are running, or for that matter playing in, how often does an antediluvian or very powerful methuselah actually appear in any capacity?<br /> <br /> For all that we (the fans of the game) talk about them a lot, how often to we actually use them in a game or do they actually appear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T10:21:17-07:00","id":1415203,"title":"","content":"Nope. And I wouldn't bring em up if other people didn't. I like that you're not supposed to know. <br /> <br /> I played one game where the ST didn't understand how rare 5th gens were supposed to be and had him as the city's Brujah sheriff (The prince was only 8th or 7th gen). That was terrifying and... Anti-climactic. I had earned his Ire and we had engage in a game of Cat and Mouse with me and The Boys taking out his supporters while doing our best to avoid him and find a weakness or a valid trap or equipment to do such a thing. We discovered the old prince had an old flintlock pistol loaded with silver specially prepared for the methuselah; then a new character completely unrelated to our shenanigans snipes the sheriff in her first game. There was tension in that he didn't die in one hit and rage-frenzied towards the shooter down the streets before getting shot again and meeting final death, but ultimately it was an assamite hit of little relation to us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T10:37:37-07:00","id":1415207,"title":"","content":"I've had Menele and Helena appear in <b>Chicago By Night</b> first edition, but they were very much background figures.<br /> <br /> I had a fifth or sixth generation two-thousand-year-old Brujah active in a modern American city (basically inspired by Critias in <b>Chicago By Night</b> and thinking he could be a much more important figure than he is in the sourcebook) and he was the &quot;sleeping giant&quot; that every other vampire tiptoed around, while he himself was happy to observe what they all did while not really thinking about the observer effect, in the style of Mithras as social Darwinist. His being a Brujah made that clan pretty smug, even though he ultimately didn't care much more about them than anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","user":"Craig Oxbrow","date":". 10-19-2021, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T12:18:59-07:00","id":1415222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use#post1415198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a game you are running, or for that matter playing in, how often does an antediluvian or very powerful methuselah actually appear in any capacity?<br /> <br /> For all that we (the fans of the game) talk about them a lot, how often to we actually use them in a game or do they actually appear?</div> </div> </div> </div>I try and make it happen less often but it happens ALL THE DAMN TIME in my games.<br /> <br /> I just can't resist GODLIKE Methuselah appears!<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm currently running the Transylvania Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T12:32:22-07:00","id":1415224,"title":"","content":"Depends on what &quot;very powerful Methuselah&quot; means.<br /> <br /> One of the eight Princes in my game is like 1200 years old. He's obviously the most powerful vampire for several hundred miles in any direction. He's a regular character who makes regular appearances, and his discipline spread reads 7/4/8/6/2/2/3.<br /> <br /> So if that would qualify, then &quot;all the time.&quot; If it doesn't, then &quot;rarely.&quot; <br /> <br /> Some of the PCs once took a trip to Athens to visit a 2500-year old Toreador who had a personal relationship with this one Sabbat Priscus that they were trying to convert back to the Camarilla. That's probably the only vampire who has ever appeared in my games who is older than the above-mentioned Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","user":"Legendre","date":". 09-23-2020, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T12:41:12-07:00","id":1415226,"title":"","content":"Never an Antedeluvian (at least not since I was a dumbass kid in the '90s), but I'll make rare use of a Methuselah. I prefer to use them as an impending sense of dread, rather than something to be directly interacted with.<br /> <br /> In a Dark Ages game I dropped conflicting rumors for months to the players that an Antedeluvian or Methuselah was entombed somewhere in the city. Threw in some random craziness with a few groups of mortals getting up and chanting &quot;The Child of Dionysus awakens&quot; and having no memory of it after the fact. Then some Assamite the group was pursuing busted into the tomb and got killed immediately. The Methuselah gave them some prophecy and pointed the group to a prophetic stele and tablet in the back of the tomb. I had a laugh when the Salubri warrior in the group turned back to ask her a question after inspecting the stele and the Methuselah was just gone. The players just had this look of dread and one of them said &quot;I don't know whether a crazy ancient Malkavian running around is a good thing or not?&quot; She basically told the group, get out of town before it's destroyed, but behind the scenes was starting to drive the Prince crazy into making bad decisions that would lead to it's destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T12:53:40-07:00","id":1415227,"title":"","content":"Ones I've used in 5th Edition:<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi<br /> Tremere/Saulot<br /> Menele<br /> Helena<br /> Keminitiri<br /> Mithras<br /> A 14th Antediluvian (albeit, it was a campaign I shared)<br /> An Amazon not based on Wonder Woman<br /> Goratrix","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T13:21:31-07:00","id":1415231,"title":"","content":"Never. I've even played through several Chicago chronicles, and the ST never used them. Though I think we may have run into Helena in a disguise once, but I think that was more of a secret easter egg than the ST doing anything with the Menele-Helena plot. All the Chicago chronicles I played were lower scaled affairs.<br /> <br /> I did start one chronicle that eventually would have lead to a globe trotting intrigue where the PCs (and various NPCs) would have discovered the lair of an ancient Brujah Methusaleh based on the Phoenician goddess Tanit who left Carthage before its fall to Rome (and was now entombed somewhere in West Africa). However, the chronicle ended (players left town for career so we decided to end the game prematurely) before that could happen. This would have been my first attempt to run a more ambitious campaign that transcended the local city stuff I've always done, and introduce a greater vampire world and levels of the Jyhad (as the Methusaleh was manipulating her descendents in all the sects - Camarilla, Anarch, and Sabbat). But it wasn't meant to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-24-2020, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T23:45:27-07:00","id":1415269,"title":"","content":"Well depends on the time place the chronicle is set. Since we are European and mostly play in European cities, there is a chance. But in modern time I try to avoid it. I put very one or two 700-1000 year old 6th gen elders in a city, they do the trick just fine. Because they begin to be alien enough for a normal vampire.<br /> <br /> I just rekindled a old campaign idea of mine, in which the players start in 9 CE as roman citizens. So they will most definitely met some Methuselah and maybe even an Ante.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T02:49:13-07:00","id":1415283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use#post1415198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a game you are running, or for that matter playing in, how often does an antediluvian or very powerful methuselah actually appear in any capacity?<br /> <br /> For all that we (the fans of the game) talk about them a lot, how often to we actually use them in a game or do they actually appear?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the chronicle. I completed a Chronicle of Ages as ST and I had antediluvians dying by the end of it. Methuselahs did appear even from early on as NPCs.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking Antes and Meths need to be used with care in any given chronicle. If you want to tell a story about the plight of the common fledgling having meths running around in the open is probably going to be counterproductive, if you are telling a story about the unspeakable secrets behind the conception of the race of Caine, meths and possibly even Antes are narrative tools you shoudl seriously consider including.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T03:03:08-07:00","id":1415284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1415227#post1415227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ones I've used in 5th Edition:<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi<br /> Tremere/Saulot<br /> Menele<br /> Helena<br /> Keminitiri<br /> Mithras<br /> A 14th Antediluvian (albeit, it was a campaign I shared)<br /> An Amazon not based on Wonder Woman<br /> Goratrix</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you run them with V5 rules or do you plot device/house rule them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T03:06:10-07:00","id":1415285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1415284#post1415284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you run them with V5 rules or do you plot device/house rule them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I go with, &quot;You die&quot; if the players attempt to attack anyone outside of a cunning plan. Like the fact that they blew up the private jet that Keminiti was on.<br /> <br /> But the absence of Elder Disciplines is my big complaint about V5.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it's my favorite rules set.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T03:10:11-07:00","id":1415286,"title":"","content":"Literally never in the past 25 years....but then I've never used a single canon character or city in my games either with the exception of a few mentions of Squizzy Taylor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T04:21:07-07:00","id":1415287,"title":"","content":"I used Arikel a bunch of time as a recurring character in two campaigns, once in Dark Ages and once in modern times, galivanting in Paris and Prague, each time passing for an ancilla.<br /> Moncada as the meat puppet of Lasombra one time.<br /> I ran the Transylvanian Chronicles, so.... quite an extensive cast of oldies.<br /> Mithras, Helena, and a Mathusalem Laibon. Triglav. The Dracon. Michael. Montano, Boukephos and Zarathustra. (quite a lot of Lasombra, I know ^^ )<br /> One of the old Salubri.<br /> Had an intervention of the Gangrel one (behind the scene) that left my players quite flustered. Kemintiri, one time.<br /> Dominic, a bunch of time. A Trujah mathusalem, too.<br /> The cast of oldies from the Tal'mahe'ra.<br /> So quite a lot, all in all. For the disciplines and general capacities, I always follow the NPC sheets if they exist, and handwave it for the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7454,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7454-darthpalpy","user":"Darthpalpy","date":". 09-24-2020, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7454-darthpalpy","name":"Darthpalpy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7454_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T09:10:34-07:00","id":1415302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1415285#post1415285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I go with, &quot;You die&quot; if the players attempt to attack anyone outside of a cunning plan. Like the fact that they blew up the private jet that Keminiti was on.</div> </div> </div> </div>During the day? Like, I don't know of the meth you're refering to, but unless they get tangled up in jet fuel or land on the Hill of Crosses* most vampires, particularly elders, can survive plane crashes (and the kinds of explosives you'd likely use in that scenario, assuming you're not strapping them to the vampire in question)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the absence of Elder Disciplines is my big complaint about V5.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it's my favorite rules set. </div> </div> </div>But so how do you work on plans that are risky but potentially workable? Or let's say your players are actually decently powerful; they have 4's and 5's in all their combat skills and disciplines, it's 3 to 1 and if we were playing another edition you could actually simulate this conflict with rules? What do you do with V5 at this point? Does the methuselah just win?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T10:18:45-07:00","id":1415304,"title":"","content":"For establishing the setting, I need to know what are their intention and if those intentions will affect the PCs. After that, I used them if needed only.<br /> <br /> I'm running Vienna, so Etrius appeared for a brief moment to the Tremere PC (he captured an inquisitor with true faith, and useful for one of Etrius rituals), and for instruction of a lesser ritual via Oneiromancy as a reward to the PC.<br /> <br /> I used Mithras for an individual prelude scene for the Ventrue PC in '91, cellar beneath Centre Point office, London (right after his rise from torpor) and Kartarirya in Colombo, Sri Lanka. The reason for the PC to be around such significant kindred is because her sire is Bindusara and this was around the time before her release.<br /> <br /> In an older chronicle I used Lambach Ruthven when the LA coterie went to NYC to warn them to stop investigating events in the city (the dread worked perfectly, they wanted to leave the city as soon as possible)<br /> <br /> In my KotE chronicle i'm using Tremere/Saulot/Tzimisce as a focal point of one of the PCs (that has 0 idea of what's going on with him after he returned from Yomi from an apparent 3rd breath) because its the last part of the chronicle that will end in the Sixth Age. Saulot will use the PC to become the Demon Emperor, but Tzimisce/Tremere know of this and will interfere. I tease with visions, dreams, and instinctive knowledge on hermeticism and the on/off presence of the PC's P'o. One of the PCs from the wu read the Heaven Scream Book in Chongqing and knows how the sixth age will unravel upon them.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 09-24-2020, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T12:49:12-07:00","id":1415310,"title":"","content":"Antediluvian never ever. Methuselah just some what never. They play a part behind the scenes, but the players are unlikely to ever encounter one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T15:10:48-07:00","id":1415328,"title":"","content":"I've had direct encounters with methuselah. It really depends on the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T15:11:33-07:00","id":1415329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1415302#post1415302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the day? Like, I don't know of the meth you're refering to, but unless they get tangled up in jet fuel or land on the Hill of Crosses* most vampires, particularly elders, can survive plane crashes (and the kinds of explosives you'd likely use in that scenario, assuming you're not strapping them to the vampire in question)</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably by stats but I think that would be incredibly undramatic and silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But so how do you work on plans that are risky but potentially workable? Or let's say your players are actually decently powerful; they have 4's and 5's in all their combat skills and disciplines, it's 3 to 1 and if we were playing another edition you could actually simulate this conflict with rules? What do you do with V5 at this point? Does the methuselah just win? </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I feel like any Kindred who walk into a fight should lose it. I mean, I won't disabuse it but my games reward PCs who are clever and punish PCs who are brute force types.<br /> <br /> But it would probably go like this:<br /> <br /> PC1: My Gangrel grows his claws and uses his Celerity 5 and Potence 3 to attack Helena repeatedly.<br /> <br /> PC2: I use my Dragonbreath shotgun Firearms 5 to shoot her in the face!<br /> <br /> PC3: I toss grenades.<br /> <br /> Me: You look upon Helena's visage and immediately turn upon one another with savage brutality. She sits back and watches you rush to defend her against your former best friends, letting out the occasional tinkle of delight, and you wonder how you could have ever wanted to destroy such a beautiful woman. You may spend Willpower to resist murdering your friends, though your heart breaks to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-24-2020, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T15:21:16-07:00","id":1415330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1415329#post1415329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I feel like any Kindred who walk into a fight should lose it. I mean, I won't disabuse it but my games reward PCs who are clever and punish PCs who are brute force types.</div> </div> </div> </div>what if they're neither clever nor using brute force?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T15:26:51-07:00","id":1415333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1415330#post1415330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> what if they're neither clever nor using brute force?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you maybe shouldn't be trying to take on a Methuseleh? *rimshot* Basically, my view of them is that they're powerful but not INVULNERABLE. There's some vampires who are basically Sauron or the Witch King and the way to take them down is rarely to fight them one-on-one. Technology and roleplaying can do more against Methuselahs than brute force.<br /> <br /> It's unlike a coterie of 13th generation types can bring down Helena but if they rat her out to the Second Inquisition and she's hit with a drone strike, maybe she'll be knocked into torpor for a century or two or maybe THEN they can finish her off.<br /> <br /> You can also do Godzilla 2 and maybe get two Methuselahs to duke it out.<br /> <br /> Mind you, Brute Force DOES work against Elders who can be trapped and don't have the resources to overcome everyone. It's just Methuselahs I use only as plot devices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-24-2020, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T05:32:19-07:00","id":1415402,"title":"","content":"I use both True Meths and Fake meths.<br /> <br /> <b>Fake Meths</b><br /> Those are vampire of more than 1000 years old but who do not have the power of a true methusaleah becuase they spended most of the time in torpor or weren\u00b4t really active thus their blood potency isn\u00b4t as high as it should be (As in my games it increases with age and has nothing to do with generation).Wich is great becuase as a ST is a tool that allows me to introduce anacronic relics that the players can interact with or plan to diablerice without being stomped or they dominating the plot<br /> <br /> My players have met one Lucien who they want to support to become a primogen to get in his good side , he is powerful but not beyond elder level.<br /> <br /> <b>True Meths</b><br /> They are really powerful even Helena who I designated to be built around mind control powers and social manouvers can tank at least 5 grenade launcher shots without diying while weakened by torpor (and you have to hit her).She deals an average of 20 levels of agravated damage per turn and shoack and average of 19 , the number of success needed to hit her is 19.<br /> <br /> Also If you have lower blood potency (wich you will have) you must make a determination roll of be unable (similar to willpower) to act against her , she can project his emotions over the city to influence it (ex increase the violence on the streets , increase population , make people more inmoral etc..) and she has a coterie of body guarss + small guerrilla of ghouls protecting her 24/7.<br /> <br /> <b>They are not unbeatable</b><br /> She is not unbeatable a coterie of elders can kill her with enough preparation , during the day vampires in my game cannot activate disciplines so she has to rely on ghouls and passive effects to protect herserlf and she has devoloped banes/curses like not being able to invade private propierty without invitation or getting depowered to elder level on sacred ground , also she is really paranoid and won\u00b4t fight unless she is 100% sure of winning (exception to this is Menele).<br /> <br /> Those weakness are exploited by two primogens to escape her influence becuase that is what the plot becomes when meths are involved , finding about their past and weaknesses to avoid becoming their pawns by making the intent slighly dangerous to the meth so in his paranoia it doesnt try to go against you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T18:21:19-07:00","id":1415634,"title":"","content":"My Dark Ages character, after many sessions and attempts, managed to get an audience with Yorak. With any luck Ill survive it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12172-vladikov","name":"Vladikov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T18:24:39-07:00","id":1415636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use#post1415198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a game you are running, or for that matter playing in, how often does an antediluvian or very powerful methuselah actually appear in any capacity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very rarely. Maybe a little more often in a Dark Ages game, but for the most part I tend to focus on those less than 1000 years old, and mainly on those under 150. If some ancient is about, they're more of a plot device than anything else. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T20:36:37-07:00","id":1415649,"title":"","content":"As storyteller I've only used a methuselah once\u2014Shaitan in a modified version of <i>The Chaos Factor</i>. It ended ambiguously, with the PCs not sure if he was destroyed in a massive explosion or just used same as cover for his exit and was laughing at the survivors. They also didn't know who he was, exactly. One character jumped to the conclusion that they'd met Set, and nothing in-game proved him wrong.<br /> <br /> As a player I've been in games where Tiamat, the Noah, Kementiri, Mithras (very briefly), and a couple of campaign-specific Setite methuselahs made appearances. No antediluvians, or even hints as to where they might be/what they might be doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T20:25:45-07:00","id":1416050,"title":"","content":"I really like the &quot;methuselah awakening under the city trope&quot;, however, it's absolutely ridiculously overused in Vampire, and often feels so silly in the New World, so I tend to avoid it, despite the fact that it appeals to me dramatically a lot.<br /> <br /> For me, it feels like stories involving very powerful vampires are much more suited to the cities of Europe and the Middle East, especially those that just breathe history. In my Cairo by night campaign, that unfortunately ended prematurely, I wouldn't have hesitated at all to use The Sleeping Lord, Angelique and other super-powerful vampires. And I do like stories set in such milieus, because the historicity of them, and the great contrasts between new and old, makes them very suited for the more mythological and epic aspects of Vampire's lore. And I do love those aspects...<br /> <br /> but I also love Americana, and we Swedes have such a powerful, albeit probably very fictionalized, image of America in our minds, thanks to decades of media portrayals. So I also very much enjoy stories set in the US, but there, I feel the focus should be on much younger vampires - an 800 year old Toreador Elder was by far the most dangerous vampire in my entire Las Vegas chronicle, for example (no one else in town was older than 300). I know lots of WoD purists will hate me now, but characters like Helena and Menele just don't work for me at all - it feels ridiculous to me that they would ever end up in the US. Why would they even risk the boat journey? But never mind the logic of it all - I don't think they fit in for <i>thematic</i> reasons. The US is so...new. Everything about it, to me as a Swede, feels new. The US, in Vampire, is for stories where you go deep into dishwasher drama with a supernatural twist, where you explore just what it means for someone to have lived for a century or two as a vampire - and that really, is sufficiently epic and thought-provoking.<br /> <br /> However, one can have the cake and eat it, perhaps. Mexico is a perfect setting for a merge between these two thematic opposites, because it feels much older than the US, and has a very compelling history, and more old architecture preserved, is more exotic than the US for my Swedish eyes, more full of mystery. Yet it's also a very modern country, with great contrast between old and new, a maze of dirty concrete houses scattered among old churches. And in Vampire, it was the capital of the Sabbat, so its easy to imagine that some very strange creatures ended up there. Yet it might also have traces of what was before, of those mysterious vampires, or their servants, whose lands the Sabbat conquered long ago. So in my current Mexico City chronicle, I've filled the city with vibrant, ambitious, very young vampires - but there's also a small but significant core of quite old elders trying to control them. And in this chronicle, I might use the sleeping methuselah plot despite my better judgement...for it just fits Mexico City's backstory in Mexico City by Night so well, and my plans for the chronicle too... so yeah, why not? And the players aren't that seasoned as Vampire players go, either, the trope might not feel as tired to them as it does for me. Let's just indulge in a classic methuselah plot. They're so cool after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T20:37:14-07:00","id":1416051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1416050#post1416050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know lots of WoD purists will hate me now, but characters like Helena and Menele just don't work for me at all - it feels ridiculous to me that they would ever end up in the US. Why would they even risk the boat journey?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always liked the answer, &quot;Because they're fleeing something older and worse in Europe.&quot;<br /> <br /> I always had the view that Menele and Helena were the most powerful Methuselahs in America but there were dozens of equally powerful ones in Europe.<br /> <br /> ...And the ones in Europe had fled from the ones in the Middle East.<br /> <br /> ...And the ones in the Middle East had fled from the ones in Africa.<br /> <br /> I also had the joke that Helena and Menele fleeing to South America was a terrible idea because South America and North America had their OWN old as shit vampires already. They only survived by luck and coincidence.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> One fun fact about my chronicles is that Mithras is actually one of the Methuselahs &quot;on the run.&quot; For all the fact he's an ancient inscrutable monster to most vampires, Mithras' 6000 year old self fled from the Middle East where he was originally worshiped as a god because older vampires chased him out of there. He's a baby compared to Ur-Shulgi and the dozen or more other TRULY ancient things back there. So he's in Britain because it is the farthest place on the continent he could get away from his enemies in the Assamites.<br /> <br /> Helena and Menele are babies compared to him.<br /> <br /> And the thing about the Middle East? I actually state that the majority of Methuselahs there date back to Babylon and the Second City. However, the Second City was founded by Ventrue after the Flood. It's where modern vampire history begins and everything else is a myth.<br /> <br /> But the thing about that? If you actually ever DID go to Africa, <i>there's 8th and 9th generation vampires older than Ur-Shulgi.</i> Ones who don't even use the same calenders as other vampires and either are liars or might date back to the days when the gods built flying cities and walked among mankind.<br /> <br /> Caine? Caine may be the first vampire.<br /> <br /> Or maybe he's just the first vampire that all the European ones are descended from. Maybe the Followers of Set are onto something that their god was a 1st Generation Vampire....but that means something else in Africa.<br /> <br /> I mean, that guy is probably lying when he says he predates homo sapiens and is a 200,000 years old.<br /> <br /> probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-30-2020, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T22:42:57-07:00","id":1416056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use#post1415198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a game you are running, or for that matter playing in, how often does an antediluvian or very powerful methuselah actually appear in any capacity?<br /> <br /> For all that we (the fans of the game) talk about them a lot, how often to we actually use them in a game or do they actually appear?</div> </div> </div> </div>Antes never Methuselas have either directly appeared or the results of their discipline use been obvious a few time, more in DA. You should really plan if you want to kill them, but then.the first rule of space flight applies: if brute force isn't working, you aren't using enough of it, or the right type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 09-30-2020, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T22:56:13-07:00","id":1416058,"title":"","content":"Antediluvian Appearances In My Games since 2000.<br /> <br /> * I admit, I did have Augustus Giovanni appear in a game set in New York City where he was going to awaken from torpor and personally bring about the Endless Night. The player characters were captured and brought to be his meals. The scene ended with an enormous flesh tentacle breaking through the floor and tearing him apart. Because Augustus Giovanni didn't check to see if the other Antediluvians were okay with his plan.<br /> <br /> * The player characters escorted &quot;Goratrix&quot; to Alamut (wrecked by the US military bombing it as a terrorist fortress) and watched him fight Ur-Shulgi. Tremere won when he revealed he and Saulot were now one.<br /> <br /> * The player characters found the Cathedral of Flesh and then, to their horror, had it politely talk to them about science and transhumanism for a night before letting them go with clouded memories.<br /> <br /> * I had a Chaos Factor Mage Game where they met Shaitan who admitted that he'd grown bored of being a monster and now just let itself be &quot;slain&quot; regularly to unite Kindred against it. The Baali existed merely to inspire Kindred to believe they had farther to fall.<br /> <br /> * Another balls to the wall Mage game based on Alan Wake had the player characters use a Correspondence 5/Spirit 5/Forces 2 ritual to send the Lasombra Antediluvian to the Sun after it destroyed a town in the Midwest and almost caused a zombie apocalypse. For years, it was canon in my games this is how the Lasombra Antediluvian met its end.<br /> <br /> * I described one of the PCs' emotional journey as being the brainwashed slave of Helena for a year. With the players permission, I said that they went about their nightly unlife and then one night a week were brainwashed into bringing people to her for her decadent blood feasts, orgies, and amusement then erased of their memories. Eventually, Menele knocked it out of them and they begged to have their memories of it erased again.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I was VERY high fantasy for awhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T01:50:02-07:00","id":1416083,"title":"","content":"I'd agree the &quot;methuselah slumbering under the city&quot; trope is more fitting for Old World cities, especially if the GM wants to use multiple methuselahs. But I think the rationales for &quot;why are such old vampires in such young cities&quot; worked pretty well in the published By Nights when we consider their methuselahs' backgrounds. <br /> <br /> * Menele faked his death and fled to the Americas to escape Helena.<br /> * Christopher Houghton fled to California after mortally embarrassing his sire. <br /> * Derrick Zeel hangs out in San Francisco because he isn't particularly involved in the Jyhad. (In my headcanon, he also masquerades as an ancilla much younger than he truly is, because advertising he's an Antediluvian's childe is asking for trouble.)<br /> * Marcus Vitel was sent to D.C. as a pawn of his sire. <br /> * Shaitan is an indigenous (debatably) vampire in Mexico City who long predates the arrival of the Conquistadors. <br /> <br /> By and large, we see that the methuselahs who wound up in American cities were losers in the Jyhad. The New World was a good place to run.<br /> <br /> Montreal, New Orleans, San Francisco, Milwaukee, New York, and Mexico City also lacked methuselah puppet-masters manipulating the city's politics. You had Shaitan and Tzimisce in the last two books, but they were largely uninvolved with the city's Kindred, even to the point of lacking character profiles and biographies. I think White Wolf did a pretty good job at establishing the &quot;methuselah slumbering under the city&quot; trope as part of the game's lore without overusing it. <br /> <br /> I thought Mexico City in particular hit upon an interesting point... just because there's a methuselah in the city doesn't mean that it's manipulating the younger Kindred as its puppets. Chicago established that trope with Helena's and Menele's Jyhad, but Helena was awake and Menele had an Auspex 6+ power that let him remain partly aware while in torpor. When Helena was asleep, she still had Prias. Both of them also went to a lot of trouble to call their various Dominated or blood-bound pawns and progeny to the city. But for a torpid methuselah who lacks Auspex 6+ and hasn't gone out of their way to preemptively establish control over the city's younger vampires, it's entirely possible for them to be non-players in the local Jyhad. There is only so much you can do from torpor. Diablerie: Britain and Diablerie: Mexico both offer good examples of this, with torpid methuselahs who aren't actually manipulating anyone and just want to be left alone. <br /> <br /> Also tying into that is towards what end a methuselah is manipulating younger vampires. Helena and Menele take a very active hand in Chicago's politics because they're trying to use the local Kindred as catspaws to kill their archrival with. Shaitain and Christopher Houghton, in contrast, don't have an archrival in the same city and exercise a much lighter hand in local politics. Christopher props up Don Sebastian and kills him when he gets a bigger crush on Jeremy, then uses the equivalent of Star Wars battle meditation to help Jeremy drive out the Sabbat, but that's really &quot;all&quot; he does. Most vampires go about their nightly unlives free of his influence, even if his actions had a profound role in the shaping of the Free State. Your average Anarch is not likely to die in a war he's instigated. <br /> <br /> Another neat example of three methuselahs engaged in an active feud was Dark Colony. You had three local elders who were pawns of methuselahs... still in Europe. Who lacked character profiles and biographies in Dark Colony, because they weren't in the region. I thought that was a really cool approach which made a lot of sense. There was no particular reason for these Roman-era methuselahs to make a dangerous journey across the Atlantic, so they didn't. None of them had actually lost their Jyhad to the same extent that Menele did against Helena. The fact those methuselahs could still exert control over their progeny from an ocean away also nicely established what old creatures and effective puppet-masters they were. I think that sort of setup should be more common in American cities than has been depicted, with princes and primogen acting out the feuds of slumbering grandsires still far away in Europe. <br /> <br /> <br /> In my games, whether I use Antediluvians or methuselahs really depends on their scale. If I were running a globe-trotting chronicle whose focus was global plots, I'd probably use super-old elders a fair bit. I tend to believe <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1340753-roleplaying-methuselah?p=1340825#post1340825\">less is more</a> with such characters, though, especially Antediluvians. PCs shoudn't run into the same one more than once, <i>maybe</i> twice, in the same chronicle. Giovanni Chronicles, for example, doesn't need the PCs to have a private meeting with Cappadocius and later witness Augustus diablerize him. Having a meeting with &quot;just&quot; Japheth works perfectly fine. There's nothing I can remember Cappadocius revealing that an old-as-dirt methuselah also couldn't. <br /> <br /> One of the classic problems with using high-powered NPCs in general is keeping the PCs' actions relevant. Transylvania Chronicles and Giovanni Chronicles were both horrible at this. I wouldn't be interested in playing either chronicle unless the GM told me they were rewriting the parts where Antediluvians showed up. It is just a waste of everyone's time to play out scenes where PCs amount to cheerleaders and bench-sitters for the GM's characters while they go off and do the cool things. <br /> <br /> There are tons of ways to avoid that, too. Make Tremere's plot to take over Goratrix's body only able to succeed with the PCs' help (or let them sabotage it). Let the PCs determine whether Augustus is able to completely diablerize Cappadocius or remain &quot;merely&quot; of the fourth generation. One of my favorite tactics in elder vs. elder fights is to have the two NPCs be roughly evenly matched, and to make PCs the x-factor that tips the scales in either direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T05:39:31-07:00","id":1416092,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3110_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3110\" data-vbnamecard=\"3110\">False Epiphany</a> : An excellent post, you brought up several points that made me reconsider my position a bit, and you inspired me, too. The only thing that still bugs me is how methuselahs can have endless personal wars against each other for thousands of years, without anyone ever prevailing. Why hasn't Helena ever managed to kill Menele, if she's had thousands of years to do it?<br /> <br /> I agree completely about the Transylvania Chronicles/Giovanni Chronicles problem. The problem is mostly due to bad writing and a lack of modern post-indie-RPG theory at the time of the writing of those books, but it's also a systems issue, where my ideal for Vampire would be a system that gives player characters at least a slim chance to defeat a methuselah (with defeat I don't necessarily mean physically though), by stacking odds in their favor cleverly enough, or utilizing the methuselah's weaknesses against it. For example, the Swedish indie vampire RPG &quot;Svart av kval, vit av lust&quot; (Black from angst, white from lust) is kind of a love letter to Vampire, but it's mechanics is all about a kind of interplay between the reliable, fearsome powers of the elders, and the short bursts of beast-powered madness that can let young vampires beat an elder into the ground. Now, Vampire need not be just like that, but I did like the &quot;self-destruct buttons&quot; that the ancient elders in <i>Lair of the Hidden</i> had, that gave the player characters a way to defeat them. If I do decide to use a methuselah in my Mexico City chronicle (probably Shaitan then?) I'll think long and hard how it should be used, and how to make sure that the PCs are still the main characters in that story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T10:50:23-07:00","id":1416131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1416092#post1416092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3110_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3110\" data-vbnamecard=\"3110\">False Epiphany</a> : An excellent post, you brought up several points that made me reconsider my position a bit, and you inspired me, too. The only thing that still bugs me is how methuselahs can have endless personal wars against each other for thousands of years, without anyone ever prevailing. Why hasn't Helena ever managed to kill Menele, if she's had thousands of years to do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely because they don't give each other many opportunities to.<br /> <br /> How many times over their millennia-long feud have they fought one another in personal combat? You had Pompeii in 67 CE and Fort Dearborn in 1812, and that's it. They primarily fight by pitting catspaws against catspaws, which is a very slow way to actually kill one another. If Menele's side had won the Council Wars by killing Lodin and installing Maldavis as prince, what would really happen? Menele would have more resources with which to search for Helena's resting place, but he and and his archrival would probably just continue to act out their feud through the primogen's battles. Eventually, Menele might manage to destroy or subvert most of Helena's pawns, at which point she'd probably decide to cut her losses and flee to somewhere else, and their Jyhad would get to play out all over again if Menele didn't manage to stop her flight. Theoretically, Menele is going to use his pawns once he's in a superior or lucky enough position to directly attack Helena's person, but the odds favor her in a confrontation against younger vampires. That's okay. Menele will try to hit her when she's most vulnerable and just keep throwing pawns at her until one of them finally manages to do the deed. But he probably won't get that many opportunities to directly attack her, because Helena will bring in more pawns after he neutralizes her previous ones, and he'll need to spend more time neutralizing these new ones. And since they're evenly matched as puppet-masters, Menele probably won't have an endless string of victories in these proxy wars, and Helena will manage to take out some of her archrival's pawns too. Menele will need to counter that. And so it'll continue to play out, over and over and over. <br /> <br /> This is a very slow and inefficient process for actually killing one's rivals, but it's also the most strategic one for an immortal being with unlimited time and whose foremost goal is to preserve their own existence. This is Methuselah 101. Don't risk your ass on the front lines when you can manipulate someone else into fighting your battles for you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did like the &quot;self-destruct buttons&quot; that the ancient elders in Lair of the Hidden had, that gave the player characters a way to defeat them. If I do decide to use a methuselah in my Mexico City chronicle (probably Shaitan then?) I'll think long and hard how it should be used, and how to make sure that the PCs are still the main characters in that story. </div> </div> </div>There are lots of ways for younger vampires to win fights against their elders. Canon has a ton of examples. Monty Coven kills Mithras after he's tired from a long torpor and exhausted from slaughtering a pack of Lupines. Lugoj kills Byelobog after he's driven into torpor by True Faith-wielding Teutonic Knights, and presumably with help from a large force of Anarchs. Gratiano attacks Lasombra while he's in torpor with another large force of Anarchs. Lair's self-destruct buttons were another neat point of vulnerability for PCs to exploit. <br /> <br /> Just as relevant is whether PCs actually need to fight the methuselah. If it's intended to be an antagonist, sure, have ways for them to kill it. But a methuselah can just as easily show up in a non-adversarial role. Japheth in Giovanni Chronicles is a dispenser of wisdom and insight to PCs. Valerianus in Vienna by Night hangs out with a neonate simply because he's lonely. Mahatma in Children of the Night guides his chosen protege towards Golconda, in hopes that doing so might allow him to obtain that same exalted state. <br /> <br /> The GM doesn't have to engineer a confrontation to give the PCs a fighting chance if the methuselah isn't actually interested in fighting, and a peaceful meeting between a PC and a methuselah can be a really fun and cool thing to play out. The PCs just have to be narratively consequential participants in the scene, whether that's through getting to influence the methuselah's actions, learning a secret or receiving some other reward as a result of their prior actions, or just enjoying a two-sided conversation with an interesting character. What's a waste of players' time is for the methuselah to show up and monologue at them or do cool things while their PCs sit and watch from the bleachers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T18:56:34-07:00","id":1462199,"title":"","content":"Considering in the last Masquerade game i was participated in the PC coterie was composed of Critias, Eletria, a 6th gen Cappadocian Inconnu monitor gone rogue, a kindred of uncertain generation claiming to be Caine (or at least the Berlin by Night/Bloodlines version) and a 7th gen Caitiff hellenistic blood sorcerer ex-anathema (that in no way whatsoever looks like he could cosplay Harry Potter in a 'con), i dare to say every f**king session of the whole chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-30-2021, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T20:25:18-07:00","id":1462208,"title":"","content":"My standard take is to always have 1 or 2 of them somewhere in the chronicle's host as a kind of Easter Egg. The PCs may find them at some point and interact, and their roles vary a lot, but they may also never encounter the thing, just some signs of its passage. But ultimately they tend to be background for the main story, either tired of the Jyhad or involved in plans so convoluted that for all practical purposes are nonexistent.<br /> <br /> Caveat: the players' actions may affect any character in the host they decide to mess with, and the &quot;Ancient Ones&quot; are no exception. They usually do not involve themselves directly, but it doesn't mean they won't throw some weight for or against the PCs. <i>Lair of the Hidden</i> fits perfectly on my style of how the interactions effectively play out.<br /> <br /> But then, I have one player that really, really, really loves to interact with important NPCs in every setting. And I'm married to her, so I have to concede sometimes. Then I have my share of games with many Methuselah appearing. I also played once a long game that went really far into the dark-HIGH-fantasy area, where I could get my fangs on enough old necks to get to 3rd gen myself. It wasn't in any way a typical VtM game except for strictly following the rules and mostly the setting, but I can't say it wasn't very fun for a time<br /> <br /> I had most 6+ Discipline powers in this single character and I can confirm: they're mostly lacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T14:27:24-07:00","id":1462324,"title":"","content":"i once had Lasombra itself 'present' in the scene via dominate. I also did a maguffin plot were the torpor'd vampire was probably Tzmisce. currently the Sabbat is secretly run by Enoch but that is more of a easter egg as to why the current Regent is doing such a good job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T16:59:12-07:00","id":1462357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use#post1415198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a game you are running, or for that matter playing in, how often does an antediluvian or very powerful methuselah actually appear in any capacity?<br /> <br /> For all that we (the fans of the game) talk about them a lot, how often to we actually use them in a game or do they actually appear?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Mage\u2026 All the Time. I once had Tremere (post transfer into Goratrix\u2019s body) crash an Order of Hermes conclave (which they conducted disguised as an Ars Magica LARP) as part of larger scheme to evade the Gehenna he saw on the Horizon now that he was stuck in a Methuselah body.<br /> <br /> Another campaign centered around an Aztec artifact stolen from Shaitan and his agents/pawns (and finally him) coming to reclaim it.<br /> <br /> My opening salvo in running Mage back when I was still a teenager involved \u201cThe Firstborn Son of Caine and Lilith\u201d released from an ancient tomb in China.<br /> <br /> Their raw power is enough to give late game Masters a run for their money and their minions provide an easy \u201csorting algorithm of evil.\u201d<br /> <br /> In Vampire? Almost nothing.<br /> <br /> My current campaign has a theoretical \u201cBigger Bad\u201d in the form of an offscreen (as in not even on the same continent) 5th Gen who\u2019s the sire/master of the \u201con camera Big Bad\u201d 6th Gen outsider to the city. Two of the Primogen are 7th Gen (and were basically neonates/ancillae who came to the New World, but the Prince (mostly a figurehead for the 7th Gen who used to be Prince but didn\u2019t want to deal with the daily drama) and other Primogen are 8th and everyone else is higher than that (most of the other \u201cranked\u201d positions are 9th-10th and all the 9th and about a third of the 10th are \u201cranked\u201d) and the entire rest of the Camarilla accounting for a slightly overcrowded 1:50k are gen 10-13.<br /> <br /> The VAST majority of what pushes my city to the brink of chaos are Gen 13+ Caitiff and thinbloods who\u2019ve been flowing into the city in ever increasing numbers starting around 1999 (Gehenna cults are all the rage among the Cam of the city and they offer disproportionate support to the Scourge to try and forestall The Time of Thin Blood).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T17:05:26-07:00","id":1462358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1462357#post1462357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Mage\u2026 All the Time...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting response, it might be the most interesting response in this thread. I am planning a MtA game for next year, and Tremere vampires are going to be the big bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T19:02:24-07:00","id":1462378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1462358#post1462358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting response, it might be the most interesting response in this thread. I am planning a MtA game for next year, and Tremere vampires are going to be the big bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually run a MtA chronicle where a faction of the Tremere, under Meerlinda's leadership, was working a truce with the goal of leaving the vampiric society entirely behind and go back to the Order of Hermes as a new House. She was directly involved into it and personally started to gather and teach newly Awakened Mages. Her long term plan was to get a safe heaven in a rebuilt Doissetep where she could focus on her studies and forget the centuries of suffering that Tremere and Goratrix cost her.<br /> <br /> My plan was to have this as something for the PCs to investigate and deal as they saw fit, but one of them straight up asked to have as Mentor the most intelligent and resourceful Master in town and be their direct apprentice in their chantry, wanting to put each and every BP necessary into it... the group ended up being her test cabal for the project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T05:01:59-07:00","id":1462549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1462358#post1462358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an interesting response, it might be the most interesting response in this thread. I am planning a MtA game for next year, and Tremere vampires are going to be the big bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wildest idea I never got around to using; the Antediluvians are the Nephandi Lords\u2026 in a case of \u201cbelief makes it real\u201d the early Nephandi learned of ancient prehistoric gods of darkness and started worshiping them. It would have literally linked the efforts of the Nephandi to awaken/release their Lords into the opening salvo of Gehenna.<br /> <br /> I had it in the works as an idea for how to wrap up wrap up my Mage campaigns with the end of the game line, but my ongoing campaign never ended so it\u2019s gone entirely unused. But maybe someone else will get an idea from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T10:20:54-07:00","id":1462898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1462378#post1462378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually run a MtA chronicle where a faction of the Tremere, under Meerlinda's leadership, was working a truce with the goal of leaving the vampiric society entirely behind and go back to the Order of Hermes as a new House. She was directly involved into it and personally started to gather and teach newly Awakened Mages. Her long term plan was to get a safe heaven in a rebuilt Doissetep where she could focus on her studies and forget the centuries of suffering that Tremere and Goratrix cost her.<br /> <br /> My plan was to have this as something for the PCs to investigate and deal as they saw fit, but one of them straight up asked to have as Mentor the most intelligent and resourceful Master in town and be their direct apprentice in their chantry, wanting to put each and every BP necessary into it... the group ended up being her test cabal for the project.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I disagree with the idea, but I wonder what is it with Meerlinda being deemed the most reasonable and nicest of the Inner Councillors. I recall a poster on this forum writing about the idea that Meerlinda would want to become human again. I replied to this that she could be a proponent for Humanity in the Camarilla. Now I read your interpretation of her. Is it her outline in WoD books, or maybe just the fact that she is a beautiful vampire woman with flowers in her hair?<br /> <br /> What exactly is the suffering of Meerlinda that came from Tremere and Goratrix? Did you make Meerlinda somehow regretful of being a Kindred? Seems to me like a strange idea, considering she used to be called Witch-Queen of England. I can't find it on the internet, but I distinctly recall she having such a moniker after she established herself in England. Can anyone confirm it, and direct where this is written? I think I read in regard to the 'good' Nightfolk of England forming a sort of alliance to attempt to counter Meerlinda's influence and actions.<br /> And her bloodline within Clan Tremere is very influential and potent; notably with Abetorius also being on the Inner Council of Seven.<br /> <br /> Did Meerlinda's faction of Tremere succeed in her goal in your chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-06-2021, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T12:24:31-07:00","id":1462916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415198-how-often-you-use?p=1462898#post1462898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I disagree with the idea, but I wonder what is it with Meerlinda being deemed the most reasonable and nicest of the Inner Councillors.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- Her suffering is the same of the entire original Council, including Etrius. Tremere abused his charisma to be an autocratic leader since they were mortals, this was the whole shtick of House Tremere when they were in the Order of Hermes. In that, Goratrix gave them a bad idea knowing he only had to convince their leader, and Tremere pushed the others to accept against their better judgement;<br /> <br /> 2- With new members of the Circle being far younger than those &quot;founders&quot; even when they were also House Tremere Mages (the Circle already had centuries as Mages), that means only two of them were already powerful Masters, members of the Circle and yet victimized by the people they trusted more, Meerlinda and Etrius;<br /> <br /> 3- Etrius is too devoted a lackey to Tremere, Blood Bond or not. He's temperamental, locked in petty fights with Goratrix, and eager to please his boss. He was like that long before undeath and never got better. So it is unreasonable to expect that level of treasonous machinations from him;<br /> <br /> 4- Meerlinda is a skilled diplomat and manipulator, including canonically making her ideas become Etrius' ideas to see them going forward. She was the main force in the efforts to broke alliances and treaties with other Kindred clans, being considered almost sole responsible for the Tremere being elevated to High Clan status. She also designed the future Camarilla with Hardestadt before again pushing Etrius to the front;<br /> <br /> 5- Finally, she's in the best position to do this or to act in any other way against the best interests of the clan, as she was ensconced in America, far away from the rest of the Circle.<br /> <br /> It is simply that canon material already makes Meerlinda clearly the most likely to act against the clan. I agree that wanting to be mortal again seems weird, she isn't a good person and was as hungry for immortality as all the others. But she was also a diplomat, willing to compromise for a good position and extremely intelligent, also the entire Circle of Seven was heavily hurt by the loss of their Avatars, it isn't just her, but she was the one in the position to make such a move as I planned. Even the Embrace of the entire House Tremere wasn't her idea, but again, Goratrix's. She proposed for them to keep a low profile instead.<br /> <br /> Divorcing herself from the others and reuniting with the Order of Hermes gives her back access to the resources of the Order and now the Traditions to search for any cure for the Curse and possible recovering of her Avatar, a place as head of her own House, and resources on the Jyhad that, although they can't be used just as she pleases, are far more versatile than anything any other Vampire has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T12:26:45-07:00","id":1462917,"title":"","content":"Meerlinda it should be noted is just as evil and wicked as the rest of the Council. Etrius has been back and forth about being a decent person even though he's as corrupt as the rest, he's the only one who feels regret.<br /> <br /> I always felt like Meerlinda was the most efficiently evil of the Big Three with no patience for Etrius and Goratrix's bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T03:54:48-07:00","id":1463083,"title":"","content":"I always had a concept of running meerlinda as the ego of the three with goterix filling the role of I'd and etrius as superego (critical rather than moral) with tremere himself as the fusion of all three with the extra layer of her being 'accept' vs etrius 'resent' and goterix 'embrace' mindset in regards to vampirism.<br /> I can see her as the nicest one or most reasonable. In my da game I had her kill mendacamina as she grew increasingly vile/unstable which she justified partially on moral grounds (the truth is she genuinely pitied and was disgusted at how hateful and twisted etrius' child became in comparison to the human she'd known). Then again her method to kill her did involve using return the heart, which strikes me as cruel but pragmatic.<br /> <br /> But I've always thought of her as more pragmatic than anything, this probably does make her less evil simply by not being as godawful as the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-08-2021, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:34:31-07:00","id":1463114,"title":"","content":"Tremere himself is a textbook example of the charismatic leader of a personality cult. I take this a lot into consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T17:57:42-07:00","id":1463270,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm mostly informed of Meerlinda by her childer and the fact that her efforts are concentrated in Washington D.C. and the East Coast of the United States. I wouldn't be surprised in the Illuminati-interpretation of the Tremere she's a big fact in transforming the USA to a superpower alongside Marcus Vitel.<br /> <br /> Peter Dorfman basically lets us know Meerlinda by her works.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Peter_Dorfman\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Peter_Dorfman</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/